+# Selected prisoner source frame: canonical executable identity
+
+Observed on `machine_id: desktop-3fevhd2-1c74096080`, 2026-10-25, CK3 1.20.0.4 / build25734779. Original evidence is retained under `C:/ck3-dynastic-esotericism-20261024/common-runtime-a13/runs/desktop-3fevhd2-1c74096080--dynastic-esotericism--R0014`. Review retained evidence by 2026-10-31.
+
+The real selected banishment preview failed in the SDK with `selected prisoner source: actual build`. The collection mailbox seeded its source frame with the global uppercase SHA, while `PrisonerQuoteSourceFrameReady12004` and the SDK selected-source contract require lowercase. The underlying executable identity was the same. This also left the native source samples numerically unqualified; successful preview values did not qualify their source.
+
+The shared mailbox now binds the actual adapter descriptor SHA through `BindPrisonerQuoteSourceExecutable12004`. This helper accepts only the known 64-character ASCII hexadecimal identity, canonicalizes its representation, and clears the binding for an unknown or malformed value. The strict native frame and SDK checks remain in force. Frame revisions, roles and query identities still come from the current collection and quote readers.
+
+The existing connected C++ fixture now uses the same helper with the actual uppercase build constant. It covers lowercase and mixed case, wrong identity, wrong length, nonhexadecimal, non-ASCII and embedded NUL inputs. The registered target serializes the production source wire; the existing `prisoner_selected_quote_source_wire_first.py` consumes that wire through the real SDK transport. The dedicated persistent workflow also runs the existing negotiated-preview fixture.
+
+Implementation is awaiting compilation, the complete workflow command group, and a new live session. These changes do not turn the original R0014 failure into a pass. Original frame/SDK/DLL remain frozen.
+
+R0014 closed with actual Game exit0, host exit1, public run2, keeper allocator0 and SCREEN release sequence8937. Its failure lifecycle completed, with normal-close and business qualification false. The actual frozen allocator failure-resource consumer returned0 for the retained 31-pin closure. This permits administrative continuation only.
+
+Detailed original diagnosis: `C:/ck3-dynastic-esotericism-20261024/R14-runtime-preparation-a13/R14-BANISH-SOURCE-FRAME-DIAGNOSIS.a01.md`, SHA256 `cc02a06698f18dd99f1fc2378c463b2539034bc4f7e49fb4afef21e7bc5c5200`. Failure closure: `C:/ck3-dynastic-esotericism-20261024/R0014-preserved-failure-close-a01/failure-close.json`, 9391 bytes, SHA256 `f564867a00a3fdc3479d1a4c9797bc59329d8b4eedb8b30d888572bf25f259fc`.
